@startuml Inspect Sensor Importance Sequence Diagram
title Figure X: Fault Detection - Inspect Sensor Importance & Explainability Sequence Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #fff9e6
    BorderColor #d4a017
    FontSize 11
}

actor "Plant Operator" as User
participant "FaultDetection UI" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "Diagnostic Engine" as Engine <<Control>>
participant "AI Model API" as AI <<External Service>>

autonumber

User -> UI : Select Active Fault (e.g., "Efficiency Drop")
User -> UI : Click "Inspect Sensor Importance"
activate UI

UI -> Engine : getSensorContribution(faultId)
activate Engine

Engine -> AI : POST /api/explain (sensor_features)
activate AI
note right of AI : Calculates Feature Importance\n(e.g., SHAP or LIME values)
AI --> Engine : { contributions: [ {sensor: 'vibration', weight: 0.8}, ... ] }
deactivate AI

Engine -> Engine : Normalize Weights to Percentages
Engine --> UI : Ranked Sensor Importance List
deactivate Engine

UI -> UI : Render Importance Chart
note right : Visualizes which sensors\ndrove the AI's decision.

UI --> User : Display Ranked Contributors (e.g., "Vibration: 80%")
deactivate UI

note right of UI
  **Explainability:**
  This process translates "Black Box"
  AI decisions into actionable 
  engineering insights for the 
  maintenance team.
end note

@enduml
